<Page title="Privacy Policy | RDB Building Services LTD" description="How the current RDB website handles information, including the local enquiry brief, external links, privacy rights and launch-stage information.">
<section class="wrap service-intro"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Privacy Policy</span></div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1></section>
<article class="wrap legal-content">
<h2>Who is responsible?</h2><p>The business responsible for this website is R D B BUILDING SERVICES LTD (trading here as RDB Building Services LTD), company number 16900008, registered in England and Wales. Its registered office is 23 Rothbury Gardens, Wallsend, United Kingdom, NE28 7DZ. For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:info@rdbbuildingservices.co.uk">info@rdbbuildingservices.co.uk</a> or write to the business location: Unit 1, Newlands Farm, Newlands Lane, The Royal Town of Sutton Coldfield, Curdworth, Sutton Coldfield B76 0BE, United Kingdom.</p>
<h2>The enquiry brief stays on your device</h2><p>The homepage enquiry tool lets you enter your name, email address, site postcode, approximate budget, service interest and project description. When you choose “Download enquiry brief”, the website creates a text file in your browser and downloads it to your device. The application does not send those fields to RDB, store them in a database, or save them in cookies, local storage or session storage.</p><p>Completing the form is optional. The browser holds the entered information while the page remains open and may retain or autofill fields according to your own browser settings. The downloaded file remains on your device until you manage or delete it. Take care when using a shared device and avoid adding unnecessary sensitive information about yourself or others.</p>
<h2>The contact page enquiry form</h2><p>The contact form also offers optional telephone and timescale fields. Choosing “Open enquiry in email” creates a mailto link containing your entered details and asks your device to open an email draft. Your email application handles that draft under its own settings. Nothing is sent to RDB automatically: you must review and send the email yourself. A download option creates a local text file instead. The contact form does not submit information to a website server or store entries in browser storage.</p><h2>Browsing information and hosting</h2><p>The current site contains no analytics, advertising pixels, embedded maps, remotely loaded fonts or third-party enquiry processor. Images, styles and application scripts are served from the website’s own files.</p><p>The website is prepared for hosting on Vercel. Delivering pages and protecting the service involves technical request information such as IP addresses, requested resources and browser or device information. Infrastructure processing is separate from optional analytics or advertising scripts, which this application does not include.</p><h2>Hosting providers and international processing</h2><p>Vercel operates a distributed infrastructure. Processing may take place outside the UK, and the applicable contractual and transfer arrangements depend on the hosting plan and service configuration. See <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel’s privacy information</a>. RDB must confirm the account’s enabled features, applicable processing terms, log retention and access arrangements; a UK business address does not mean that all website data stays in the UK.</p><h2>Retention details still to be confirmed</h2><p>The enquiry tool has no server-side record to retain: you control the file it downloads. Retention periods for hosting logs, correspondence and customer records are not yet confirmed. RDB must set appropriate periods or clear criteria for each purpose and update this notice before launch; no universal retention period is stated here.</p><h2>Messages sent outside this website</h2><p>The website provides an email link to <a href="mailto:info@rdbbuildingservices.co.uk">info@rdbbuildingservices.co.uk</a>, but has no form submission endpoint. Following an email link opens your own email application; it does not send a message automatically. If you send a brief or contact RDB by email or post, RDB will receive the information you share. RDB must confirm the email provider, processing purposes and lawful bases, recipients and retention periods in this notice before public launch.</p><p>Typical purposes may include responding to a requested quotation and administering an agreed project, but the business must confirm its actual practices. This notice does not give permission to use enquiry information for unrelated marketing.</p>
<h2>External links</h2><p>Maps and official guidance open as links to separate websites. They are not embedded in the page. If you choose to visit them, those providers handle information under their own privacy notices. RDB does not send the details entered in the enquiry tool as part of these links.</p>
<h2>Your choices and rights</h2><p>Where RDB processes your personal information, UK data protection law may give you rights to access, correct or erase information, restrict processing, object, or request portability. Which rights apply depends on the circumstances and lawful basis. Where processing relies on consent, you can withdraw it without affecting earlier lawful processing.</p><p>Email <a href="mailto:info@rdbbuildingservices.co.uk">info@rdbbuildingservices.co.uk</a> or write to the business address above to ask a question or exercise a right. Requests should normally receive a response within one month, subject to applicable legal provisions. If you are concerned about how your information is handled, you can also complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Information Commissioner’s Office</a>.</p>
<h2>Cookies and changes to this notice</h2><p>See the <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> for the current application’s use of browser storage. This notice will need to be revised if hosting, analytics, messaging, payments or other data processing features are added. </p>
</article></Page>
